disney's peter pan has been loved by  families for generations  unfortunately this animated classic  hasn't aged entirely well  over the years much of this goes over  kids heads but older viewers might be  surprised by some scenes  for good or bad here are things that  only adults notice in peter pan  as a child it feels perfectly innocent  to fantasize about some magical being  coming to your window to take you away  on adventures in faraway lands  as an adult however the thought of  strange boys visiting underage daughters  via bedroom windows  is much less charming when wendy claims  peter pan has been to the nursery before  and must surely be coming again because  she'd found his shadow her mother seems  a bit perplexed  her father on the other hand brushes it  off as childish fiddle fattle and mocks  his wife's concern  goodness gracious whatever shall we do  however had the same conversation been  with more literal or protective  guardians  peter likely would have found a father  waiting with his shotgun  in that nursery instead of a pining  unattended wendy  at the very least it would have been  wise to leave the family dog nana in the  house with the kids  rather than tied up outside on top of  that the grown mind can't help but  question mr and mrs darling's decision  to leave their young children home alone  for hours without any sort of adult  supervision  if you're not going to have your dog  protect your children while you're out  partying at least  find a human to babysit fairies are some  of the most iconic creatures in the  worlds of fantasy but their disposition  varies widely between sources  in some instances they're benevolent and  wise like cinderella's fairy godmother  while other portrayals of the magical  beings  show a much darker and malevolent nature  peter pan's sidekick tinkerbell seems to  lie somewhere in the middle  tink displays a mean jealous streak the  moment she learns wendy will be  accompanying them back to neverland  going so far as to make an attempt on  her life without peter's knowledge  after abandoning wendy while flying to  peter's hideout hangman's tree  tinkerbell tells the awaiting lost boys  that he gave orders to shoot down a  terrible wendy bird  spotted in the skies sadly the lost boys  followed tinker bell's instructions and  attack her but peter manages to fly over  just in time to save wendy from crashing  down  onto the jagged rocks below when peter  asks tinkerbell if she's guilty or not  guilty of attempting to get wendy shot  down she has an  honest and disturbing response guilty  don't you know you might have killed her  after being banished for her malicious  plot tink makes things even worse by  turning on peter disclosing his hideout  to his  arch-nemesis captain hook thankfully she  redeems herself in the end by saving  peter from a bomb that hook disguises as  a gift but still  it doesn't excuse tink's attempt to  plant wendy's six feet under  being a child forever sounds pretty  liberating on the surface but when  examined more deeply it definitely has a  dark side  while infantile behavior brings carefree  fun and spontaneity it can also  cultivate a short-sighted and selfish  nature this is exhibited time and time  again by peter pan who repeatedly puts  others in danger thanks to his immature  actions and motives  from the moment he's introduced he  constantly makes everything about  himself  as a kid it's easy to mistake peter's  decision to take wendy and her brothers  to neverland as a form of liberation and  a heroic rescue from growing up  which george tells wendy she'll have to  do starting the next day by moving out  of the nursery with her brothers and  into her own room  however more mature viewers are apt to  note that peter only invites them to  neverland because wendy's imminent  relocation would put an end to her  adventure stories  and peter truly loves these tales  because they're about him  but the character's dark side doesn't  stop there peter also treats all the  females in his life like trinkets rather  than people quickly moving on to the  next shiny thing in front of him like  when he leaves wendy behind for tiger  lily  to top it off he occasionally drops  misogynistic insights and demands that  haven't aged well  at all girls talk too much yes  girls talk to them oh well  get on with it girl my name is wendy  when watching peter pan adult viewers  can't help but notice disturbing levels  of racism in the classic film  it's so bad that disney plus even added  a disclaimer before the film warning  viewers about  quote negative depictions and or  mistreatment of people or cultures  not only does this film depict native  americans in horrifically prejudiced  ways  the movie is carpet bombed with racist  slurs against them  everyone from innocent children and the  heroic pan to the villainous captain  hook  casually speak of them as savages and  much worse  the poor treatment of native americans  and other first nations people  culminates in a sing-along titled what  makes the red man red which is loaded  with cultural appropriation  and racist stereotypes early in the film  we learned that captain hook has a  perfectly viable reason for being so  upset with peter pan  after all he's responsible for hook  having a hook in the first place  during a skirmish with the villain peter  cut off hook's hand  and fed it to a nearby crocodile who  then developed a taste for the pirate  leader's flesh  as a result the crocodile constantly  haunts captain hook and follows him  around neverland hoping for another  nibble  luckily the crocodile also swallowed a  clock so he can be easily detected by  the distinctive sound of ticking  emanating from his tummy  hook's encounters with the crocodile  make for some of the funniest moments in  the film  but it also stirs up some questions  within the discerning adult mind  specifically one can't help but wonder  why hook doesn't just organize a group  of his men to execute the beast so he no  longer has to live in perpetual fear  he's a badass pirate captain in charge  of a ship loaded with dangerous men  cannons and other weapons he should put  those to good use against the crocodile  so he can move on with his life  plus the croc doesn't seem to be too  elusive or quick moving  however like most kids adults should  overlook this leap in logic and enjoy  the timeless comedy of these two  fighting it out  an uncomfortable aspect of peter pan  comes into focus when analyzing the  questionable relationship between peter  and wendy  the two technically meet for the first  time after he breaks into the nursery  window at night while her parents are  out  which is unnerving enough however peter  had to have been there at least once  before while she was sleeping  considering wendy found his misplaced  shadow in the nursery  which definitely amps up the creep  factor then things get even more  uncomfortable  while considering the weighty decision  of whether she should go with a stranger  to a strange land  wendy wonders aloud what her mother will  think peter being unwise in the ways of  the world  asks wendy what a mother is to which she  replies  a mother's someone who who loves and  cares for you  and tells you stories good you can be  our mother  moments after this statement wendy  declares she's so excited to see peter  that she's going to give him a kiss  and not in the motherly sort of way this  has some weird freudian connotations to  say the least and it sets a bit of an  odd  undertone between the two throughout the  rest of the film  in the latter half of the movie wendy  sings a touching song called your mother  and mine  it's a sweet melody praising motherly  love soothing enough to lull her rowdy  brothers and the lost boys into a  relaxed blissful state  wendy's song even brings the pirates to  tears one pirate in particular mr smee  captain hook's comical boson is shown  crying while pulling up his shirt to  reveal a classic mom tattoo on his chest  making this one of the film's more  memorable and humorous moments  even tough guys love their mamas and  when watching this scene as an adult it  genuinely pulls on the heartstrings and  makes shmi's actions far more relatable  as a kid it's easy to take songs about  mothers for granted but once you've  moved out on your own your mom  isn't as easily accessible and distance  makes the heart grow fonder  more than a few adults watching this  movie probably found themselves getting  misty during this touching tribute to  mothers everywhere  they say you should never meet your  heroes and for those who idolize  mermaids this is particularly true while  watching peter pan  mermaids are generally depicted as  friendly benevolent creatures  especially in such films as splash or  the little mermaid however neverland's  resident  merfolk have darker natures which wendy  learns to her detriment while exploring  the island with peter  as it turns out peter is quite the  ladies man and  wendy finds herself vying for his  attention while he catches up with  fangirling mermaids in a neverland  lagoon  once they notice wendy however the  mermaids switch from flirtatious vixens  to jealous tyrants  while peter looks on laughing the  mermaids attempt to pull her under the  water  this is the second time wendy nearly  meets her fate at the hands of one of  peter's female friends  and like tinkerbell the mermaids own up  to their true intentions  in sociopathic like fashion the mermaids  acknowledge  exactly what they were trying to do we  were only trying to drown her  after losing his temper early in the  film george darling takes his  frustrations out on nana the canine  nanny by  banishing the poor dog outside to her  lonely drafty dog house  it's sadly ironic as she's the least  chaotic and most helpful member of the  entire family  this is extra cruel considering she's  not just any dog  nana thinks of herself as a nursemaid  and that she belongs  inside watching over the children she  does all the things a traditional  caretaker would  modifying some activities to accommodate  her lack of opposable thumbs  it's hard not to marvel at her  incredible dexterity and ability to  carry out a multitude of domestic tasks  even professionally trained dogs could  learn a thing or two from nana's  extensive skill set  and yet the darling family seems to take  her entirely for granted  for example while george's angrily  pacing about  making a scene over his outfit nana  continually tries to clean up and care  for the kids in the background  nana is so loyal that when george  struggles to find the rope to tie her up  outside  she pauses mid-banishment to find it for  him while she's just another humorous  character for kids to enjoy many adults  watching the film probably wish they  could have their own nana around the  house  although some of peter pan's content  hasn't aged too well  one of its spin-off movies more than  stands the test of time  directed by steven spielberg 1991's hook  imagines a life where peter falls in  love with wendy's granddaughter moira  and leaves neverland to start a family  of his own it's a heartwarming fantasy  featuring a stellar cast  including robin williams as peter pan  dustin hoffman as captain hook and julia  roberts as tinkerbell  ironically the once carefree boy grows  into an incredibly stiff-necked  workaholic with a fear of heights  he's also too busy climbing the  corporate ladder to spend any quality  time with his kids  but daily life is interrupted for  peter's family when captain hook kidnaps  his children and takes them back to  neverland  peter is forced to face his past in  order to save his family's future  in the process he remembers what's truly  important in life  reconnects with his inner child and  finds redemption with his loved ones  it's a grand adventure exploring a  boldly reimagined neverland but  it's also loaded with fun callbacks to  the 1953 classic  granted critics weren't especially fond  of it when it first hit theaters but  nevertheless hook is a joyous  family-friendly ride  plus the special effects still hold up  the musical score is excellent  and best of all the movie doesn't  contain any of the outdated and cringy  moments that only adults would notice  from the original animated version  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite classic movies are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

